<title>UK: APS buys Johnson airport manager unit.</title>
<headline>APS buys Johnson airport manager unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based American Port Services Plc said on Monday it had signed an agreement to buy the key contracts of U.S. small commercial airports manager Johnson Controls Aviation Services from Johnson Controls Inc for $18.75 million.</p>
<p>APS said the airports managed by Johnson Controls Aviation Services handle approximately 16 million passengers a year, with around 700,000 aircraft operations.</p>
<p>APS said the contracts generate revenues of $38 million and the division has net assets of around $10 million.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
